<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan BSPA buys 54,000 tonnes Brazil soybeans.</title>
<headline>Taiwan BSPA buys 54,000 tonnes Brazil soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kaohsiung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of Brazilian soybeans from Louis Dreyfus Corp at a tender on Tuesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The breakfast association's Kaohsiung division comprises Great Wall Enterprise, Ttet Union, President Enterprise and Tai Hwa Oil.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Type	 Tonnes   Date/Location  Prices/Future</p>
<p>			   Brazil port</p>
<p> Brazilian  54,000   July 1-20	40.38 US cents/July</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
